1
00:01:28,144 --> 00:01:33,950
TRUNK BUDDIES

2
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:39,756
I'll stay at the amusement arcade until 10:30...

3
00:01:39,956 --> 00:01:42,992
No, let's make that 11:00.

4
00:01:43,460 --> 00:01:44,994
What are you doing?

5
00:01:45,195 --> 00:01:48,832
Oh, it's you, Nakagawa. I thought it was Chief Ohara.

6
00:01:49,032 --> 00:01:50,300
Tomorrow is my day off.

7
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:53,837
So I'm making a detailed schedule for a productive day.

8
00:01:54,037 --> 00:01:56,539
You're so meticulous outside of work.

9
00:01:56,773 --> 00:01:58,241
Of course.

10
00:01:58,575 --> 00:02:00,543
Too few off-duty days relative to workdays.

11
00:02:01,244 --> 00:02:03,980
I want five days off a week like most people.

12
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:06,149
The average person gets two days off a week.

13
00:02:06,349 --> 00:02:09,319
I work hard to ensure the safety of citizens.

14
00:02:09,519 --> 00:02:11,254
It's a reasonable request.

15
00:02:11,488 --> 00:02:14,057
You act like you have seven days off a week anyway.

16
00:02:16,259 --> 00:02:19,529
But to keep to this strict schedule,

17
00:02:19,729 --> 00:02:21,865
I need the stamina of an iron man.

18
00:02:24,067 --> 00:02:26,136
Hello, this is Kameari...

19
00:02:26,336 --> 00:02:27,737
Huh, what?

20
00:02:27,971 --> 00:02:31,708
I'll take a break here to have lunch and a pee...

21
00:02:31,908 --> 00:02:33,009
Ryotsu, we have a problem!

22
00:02:33,343 --> 00:02:34,177
Huh?

23
00:02:36,012 --> 00:02:37,413
-What's wrong? -What happened?

24
00:02:37,614 --> 00:02:39,182
-It's an elephant. -Unbelievable!

25
00:02:41,584 --> 00:02:43,420
It's dangerous! Please stay back!

26
00:02:43,620 --> 00:02:45,088
Move back, please!

27
00:02:45,288 --> 00:02:48,892
-It's dangerous. -Hey, don't enter!

28
00:02:49,092 --> 00:02:51,261
No one is allowed in the store.

29
00:02:51,461 --> 00:02:53,930
-Keep your distance. -It's dangerous.

30
00:02:54,164 --> 00:02:56,699
This is what'll happen if it steps on you!

31
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:58,568
Coming through.

32
00:02:58,768 --> 00:03:00,470
-Wow, look at that. -You're late!

33
00:03:00,703 --> 00:03:02,739
-Sorry to be late. -Nakagawa-san!

34
00:03:02,939 --> 00:03:04,574
-Anyone injured? -No one.

35
00:03:05,041 --> 00:03:06,876
So, where's the elephant?

36
00:03:12,749 --> 00:03:14,484
It's in the back storage room.

37
00:03:14,884 --> 00:03:17,187
Just go and catch it already!

38
00:03:17,387 --> 00:03:18,721
You're used to it, right?

39
00:03:18,922 --> 00:03:21,191
Why would I be used to an elephant?

40
00:03:21,391 --> 00:03:24,227
-I'll go in too. -Please don't. It's dangerous.

41
00:03:24,427 --> 00:03:26,262
Hey, that's discrimination!

42
00:03:26,462 --> 00:03:29,032
It's differentiation. Get on with it!

43
00:03:30,733 --> 00:03:31,634
Please take this.

44
00:03:31,868 --> 00:03:33,503
I don't need it.

45
00:03:44,447 --> 00:03:46,916
Oh, it's just a baby elephant.

46
00:03:48,451 --> 00:03:50,887
Easy, elephant, you'll be okay.

47
00:03:58,995 --> 00:04:01,297
It's so quiet. Is he all right?

48
00:04:04,701 --> 00:04:05,535
Ryotsu!

49
00:04:05,768 --> 00:04:08,071
It's dangerous, Nakagawa-san!

50
00:04:10,173 --> 00:04:11,975
Hey, let me go! Argh!

51
00:04:14,277 --> 00:04:15,345
Release Ryotsu!

52
00:04:29,559 --> 00:04:32,562
-Bring milk and a baby bottle right now! -What?

53
00:04:32,795 --> 00:04:34,464
-Hurry up! -Y-Yes!

54
00:04:35,098 --> 00:04:35,965
Oh, Nakagawa-san!

55
00:04:36,165 --> 00:04:37,166
Nakagawa-san.

56
00:04:37,367 --> 00:04:39,335
I'm so glad you're safe.

57
00:04:39,536 --> 00:04:41,871
Excuse me, do you have milk and a baby bottle?

58
00:04:42,105 --> 00:04:42,939
Huh?

59
00:04:46,843 --> 00:04:49,712
There, there. It's okay. Don't be scared.

60
00:04:49,946 --> 00:04:51,481
First, we'll fill its stomach.

61
00:04:51,681 --> 00:04:53,149
That'll probably calm it down.

62
00:04:53,650 --> 00:04:55,051
There, there.

63
00:04:55,285 --> 00:04:57,420
What's taking so long? You're so clumsy.

64
00:04:58,221 --> 00:04:59,188
It's ready!

65
00:05:00,657 --> 00:05:02,325
Do you think it'll drink it?

66
00:05:02,525 --> 00:05:04,761
Milk is the basic food for mammals.

67
00:05:04,994 --> 00:05:06,829
Here's your milk.

68
00:05:12,335 --> 00:05:14,170
It's from a cow, but it's all we have.

69
00:05:14,370 --> 00:05:17,740
Look, drink it like this.

70
00:05:20,243 --> 00:05:22,178
Got it? Now you.

71
00:05:22,512 --> 00:05:23,913
Drink it.

72
00:05:28,518 --> 00:05:29,352
It's drinking!

73
00:05:29,552 --> 00:05:32,989
Okay. Good baby, good baby.

74
00:05:39,095 --> 00:05:41,431
The elephant...!

75
00:05:42,365 --> 00:05:44,567
Don't make a fuss. You'll scare it.

76
00:05:45,568 --> 00:05:48,371
It's okay. Don't be afraid.

77
00:05:49,939 --> 00:05:52,208
It's completely attached to Ryotsu.

78
00:05:52,408 --> 00:05:54,210
They're both wild animals.

79
00:05:54,611 --> 00:05:56,479
It's big, but still a baby.

80
00:05:56,713 --> 00:05:59,415
If you don't excite it, it'll be quiet.

81
00:05:59,616 --> 00:06:02,085
But where could it have come from?

82
00:06:02,285 --> 00:06:05,488
I doubt anyone was keeping it as a pet.

83
00:06:05,722 --> 00:06:08,925
And it couldn't have swam all the way here from Africa.

84
00:06:09,125 --> 00:06:12,195
-So, it must be from a zoo. -I see.

85
00:06:12,762 --> 00:06:14,931
Please keep it here until someone picks it up.

86
00:06:15,131 --> 00:06:16,199
Let's go, Nakagawa.

87
00:06:16,399 --> 00:06:18,801
Come on, officer, give me a break!

88
00:06:21,771 --> 00:06:23,773
I can't breathe! Nakagawa!

89
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:29,045
It won't let go of you!

90
00:06:29,412 --> 00:06:30,913
A beast and an elephant.

91
00:06:31,114 --> 00:06:33,149
What a lovely couple.

92
00:06:38,588 --> 00:06:40,089
Why is an elephant here?

93
00:06:40,289 --> 00:06:43,292
Apparently, he was lost. So, Ryo-chan picked him up.

94
00:06:43,793 --> 00:06:45,495
Why is he in the police station?

95
00:06:46,062 --> 00:06:49,799
If I tie him outside and he tramples a drunk guy, it'll be a problem.

96
00:06:49,999 --> 00:06:52,502
We have no choice but to keep him here until morning.

97
00:06:52,702 --> 00:06:56,005
Ryo-chan was so kind that he's gotten quite attached to him.

98
00:06:56,339 --> 00:06:59,008
Ryotsu is liked by all but humans.

99
00:06:59,809 --> 00:07:01,511
Not for me!

100
00:07:01,844 --> 00:07:02,679
See?

101
00:07:02,879 --> 00:07:05,848
Wow, a real elephant! It's huge!

102
00:07:06,082 --> 00:07:07,850
I'll let you ride him for 100 yen.

103
00:07:08,084 --> 00:07:09,685
Wow, really?!

104
00:07:10,086 --> 00:07:11,087
Ryotsu!

105
00:07:11,287 --> 00:07:13,189
Just kidding. They can ride for free.

106
00:07:13,423 --> 00:07:14,190
Go ahead.

107
00:07:14,624 --> 00:07:16,459
Yay! Put me on his back!

108
00:07:16,659 --> 00:07:18,694
Very well. Here you go.

109
00:07:19,429 --> 00:07:21,364
Wow, this is awesome!

110
00:07:21,564 --> 00:07:23,166
It's so high!

111
00:07:25,334 --> 00:07:27,136
He gave me some grass.

112
00:07:27,336 --> 00:07:28,504
Yeah, he did.

113
00:07:29,672 --> 00:07:32,141
Has anyone filed a missing elephant's report?

114
00:07:32,341 --> 00:07:35,745
I reported it to HQ, but so far, nothing yet.

115
00:07:35,978 --> 00:07:40,016
Well, if he gets grumpy, give him another bottle of milk.

116
00:07:40,516 --> 00:07:42,518
Surely you're not going home?

117
00:07:42,719 --> 00:07:43,519
What?

118
00:07:45,154 --> 00:07:46,522
-Ryotsu! -Ryo-chan!

119
00:07:46,723 --> 00:07:48,224
What the heck?

120
00:07:50,226 --> 00:07:52,528
Don't look at me like that!

121
00:07:53,196 --> 00:07:55,064
My shift is over,

122
00:07:55,298 --> 00:07:57,300
so I'm off-duty until the end of tomorrow.

123
00:07:57,733 --> 00:07:59,902
You'll just lie around all day anyway.

124
00:08:00,136 --> 00:08:02,772
Why don't you take care of him until someone picks him up?

125
00:08:03,139 --> 00:08:04,006
No can do.

126
00:08:05,241 --> 00:08:06,609
W-What's this?

127
00:08:06,843 --> 00:08:09,612
His off-duty schedule for tomorrow.

128
00:08:09,846 --> 00:08:11,747
It's packed to the minute.

129
00:08:12,215 --> 00:08:16,319
9:00 get up, 9:03 breakfast, 9:30 plastic model shop,

130
00:08:16,519 --> 00:08:19,589
10:00 amusement arcade, 10:45 second breakfast...

131
00:08:19,789 --> 00:08:23,426
-It's late, so you should go home. -Okay!

132
00:08:23,626 --> 00:08:25,261
...12:00 lunch.

133
00:08:25,628 --> 00:08:27,230
I'm too busy to do it.

134
00:08:27,430 --> 00:08:29,432
Why're you only organized for stupid things?

135
00:08:29,799 --> 00:08:31,200
He's your responsibility.

136
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:34,237
You brought him here, so you need to look after him.

137
00:08:34,437 --> 00:08:35,505
That's right.

138
00:08:35,972 --> 00:08:37,440
This is not my elephant.

139
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:40,643
I didn't bring him. He followed me on his own.

140
00:08:40,877 --> 00:08:44,046
I won't waste my precious day off on something like this!

141
00:08:44,247 --> 00:08:45,515
Good night.

142
00:08:48,050 --> 00:08:48,885
See you!

143
00:09:00,830 --> 00:09:03,399
I'm going home no matter what!

144
00:09:03,966 --> 00:09:05,835
I don't care what anyone says...

145
00:09:07,670 --> 00:09:10,439
Hey, let me go.

146
00:09:10,640 --> 00:09:12,408
He's not going to leave you.

147
00:09:12,608 --> 00:09:14,944
Why don't you take him with you, Ryo-chan?

148
00:09:15,411 --> 00:09:16,546
Don't be silly!

149
00:09:16,746 --> 00:09:19,549
Take him home! That's an order from your chief.

150
00:09:21,551 --> 00:09:24,554
"NIKONIKO DORMITORY"

151
00:09:24,754 --> 00:09:28,324
W-What's that big thing?

152
00:09:28,558 --> 00:09:32,562
Chief Ohara ordered me to bring him, so blame him if there's a problem.

153
00:09:41,470 --> 00:09:43,973
I just cleaned the floor.

154
00:09:44,173 --> 00:09:46,042
Don't walk with dirty feet!

155
00:09:46,275 --> 00:09:47,677
Fine, I'll wash his feet.

156
00:09:53,049 --> 00:09:54,684
Excuse us, everyone.

157
00:09:55,017 --> 00:09:56,686
What are you doing, Ryo-san?

158
00:09:56,886 --> 00:09:58,654
Don't bring an elephant into the bathroom.

159
00:09:58,854 --> 00:10:02,425
This is the dorm lady's order. If you have a complaint, tell her.

160
00:10:06,729 --> 00:10:07,730
All right.

161
00:10:09,165 --> 00:10:10,900
Okay, the other one.

162
00:10:12,868 --> 00:10:14,971
Now, the back ones.

163
00:10:16,706 --> 00:10:18,074
Good, they're all clean.

164
00:10:18,307 --> 00:10:20,910
Listen, just wait here quietly.

165
00:10:23,079 --> 00:10:26,682
He seems to understand only what I say.

166
00:10:35,157 --> 00:10:37,360
He doesn't understand you at all, Ryo-san.

167
00:10:45,468 --> 00:10:48,037
You'd better not turn over in your sleep.

168
00:11:02,084 --> 00:11:04,020
-What happened? -Look!

169
00:11:11,794 --> 00:11:14,864
You brat! That's my breakfast!

170
00:11:16,565 --> 00:11:18,868
What are you gonna do about our breakfasts?

171
00:11:19,068 --> 00:11:21,904
This is all because you brought in an elephant.

172
00:11:22,104 --> 00:11:24,407
If you're the owner, take responsibility!

173
00:11:24,607 --> 00:11:27,209
I'm telling you, this is not my elephant!

174
00:11:27,410 --> 00:11:29,979
Do something about it, Ryo-san!

175
00:11:30,379 --> 00:11:33,516
Listen! Just send someone to pick him up at once!

176
00:11:33,950 --> 00:11:37,987
No one's reported that they're missing an elephant yet.

177
00:11:38,554 --> 00:11:42,792
Then, where did he come from? Is he a stray elephant?

178
00:11:42,992 --> 00:11:44,760
If so, call the public health center!

179
00:11:45,294 --> 00:11:48,631
Anyway, I'll contact you as soon as I get any information.

180
00:11:48,831 --> 00:11:50,766
So until then, please look after him.

181
00:11:51,467 --> 00:11:55,638
All these people are trying to take advantage of my good nature!

182
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:15,157
Serves you right! I'm going straight to the plastic model shop at 9:30!

183
00:12:19,829 --> 00:12:22,932
-Ryo-san, I have that one in stock. -Great!

184
00:12:23,466 --> 00:12:26,268
The Douglas A-1 Skyraider by Morogram.

185
00:12:27,737 --> 00:12:29,872
Oh, this is the one I wanted.

186
00:12:30,573 --> 00:12:31,974
It's 8,000 yen.

187
00:12:32,441 --> 00:12:34,677
Oh, I left my wallet in the dorm.

188
00:12:34,877 --> 00:12:37,146
Don't say that again.

189
00:12:37,346 --> 00:12:40,483
No, it's true. I'll bring the money next time.

190
00:12:41,984 --> 00:12:43,285
Ryo-san!

191
00:12:48,591 --> 00:12:49,892
He's here already.

192
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:52,061
Back door is this way, right?

193
00:12:52,294 --> 00:12:54,430
Hold it! Not on credit, Ryo-san.

194
00:12:54,630 --> 00:12:57,666
Two other people have been asking for it.

195
00:12:57,867 --> 00:12:59,435
Bring the money if you want it.

196
00:13:00,036 --> 00:13:01,370
That's so cruel!

197
00:13:01,604 --> 00:13:03,906
I'll pay you, I promise. Just don't sell it.

198
00:13:04,140 --> 00:13:05,141
Please don't!

199
00:13:05,341 --> 00:13:06,609
No promises.

200
00:13:12,081 --> 00:13:14,050
I won't let him catch me.

201
00:13:23,826 --> 00:13:25,795
What are you, a police dog?

202
00:13:26,862 --> 00:13:30,566
Why do I have to go on a date with an elephant on my day off?

203
00:13:36,105 --> 00:13:37,573
Stay away! I don't know you.

204
00:13:38,507 --> 00:13:41,077
All that running has made me thirsty.

205
00:13:48,584 --> 00:13:51,253
Damn, if only I had ten more yen...

206
00:13:51,921 --> 00:13:53,422
Ten more yen.

207
00:13:53,656 --> 00:13:55,758
Oh, there's the Chunky Grape!

208
00:13:56,559 --> 00:13:59,028
The Chunky Grape...

209
00:14:02,865 --> 00:14:04,300
The Chunky...

210
00:14:05,968 --> 00:14:06,936
Ten yen.

211
00:14:11,107 --> 00:14:13,976
For small amounts of coins, even if reported to the police,

212
00:14:14,210 --> 00:14:16,846
it's difficult to identify the owner.

213
00:14:17,046 --> 00:14:19,248
I'll sort it out when I get back to the station.

214
00:14:19,448 --> 00:14:22,318
Good job, well done.

215
00:14:22,551 --> 00:14:24,954
Let's buy the Chunky Grape.

216
00:14:26,088 --> 00:14:27,790
Oh no! I pushed the Sweet Red Bean Soup!

217
00:14:27,990 --> 00:14:30,693
Who wants to drink bean soup when they're thirsty?

218
00:14:30,893 --> 00:14:32,995
Give me back my 100 yen, you jerk!

219
00:14:39,735 --> 00:14:40,970
What? Two bonus drinks?

220
00:14:41,170 --> 00:14:42,972
"SWEET RED BEAN SOUP"

221
00:14:43,405 --> 00:14:45,474
Give me something else instead.

222
00:14:47,810 --> 00:14:50,246
Now I'm even more thirsty.

223
00:14:51,113 --> 00:14:52,915
It's a pain to go back for my wallet.

224
00:14:53,115 --> 00:14:55,651
I'll cancel my plan to go to the arcade at 10 o'clock.

225
00:14:55,885 --> 00:14:58,187
Because of you, I missed breakfast,

226
00:14:58,420 --> 00:15:01,257
and you've ruined my off-duty schedule.

227
00:15:05,794 --> 00:15:07,830
Now, what should we do?

228
00:15:08,931 --> 00:15:10,332
You picked up something else?

229
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:12,568
It's a wallet.

230
00:15:12,768 --> 00:15:14,336
And it's heavy.

231
00:15:15,471 --> 00:15:17,006
It's full of money!

232
00:15:18,474 --> 00:15:20,009
Oh, that wallet!

233
00:15:20,476 --> 00:15:21,844
I've been looking for it.

234
00:15:22,044 --> 00:15:24,480
Thank you very much.

235
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:27,016
How do I know this is yours?

236
00:15:27,383 --> 00:15:30,519
I believe there's a picture of me and my granddaughter inside.

237
00:15:31,453 --> 00:15:35,024
Unfortunately, that's all the proof I have.

238
00:15:36,592 --> 00:15:40,129
I don't recommend carrying around a lot of money.

239
00:15:40,329 --> 00:15:42,631
Thank you. I'll be careful.

240
00:15:42,831 --> 00:15:45,034
I must say, that's an unusual pet.

241
00:15:45,701 --> 00:15:48,871
Many Asian countries have traditionally regarded elephants as gods

242
00:15:49,071 --> 00:15:52,308
and have cherished them for a long time.

243
00:15:52,508 --> 00:15:54,009
A god? This one?

244
00:15:54,210 --> 00:15:56,345
I'm sorry it's not much,

245
00:15:56,545 --> 00:15:58,647
but please use this to feed your elephant.

246
00:15:59,014 --> 00:16:00,883
What? This much?

247
00:16:01,383 --> 00:16:04,386
I think it's customary to give 10% as a reward.

248
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:06,388
Have a nice day.

249
00:16:06,622 --> 00:16:09,391
I-I got 30,000 yen!

250
00:16:12,261 --> 00:16:13,829
Looks like we're in luck.

251
00:16:14,029 --> 00:16:16,398
Which means we're back on schedule for the afternoon.

252
00:16:16,632 --> 00:16:19,068
Follow me, God!

253
00:16:20,102 --> 00:16:22,538
"KAMEARI STATION NORTH EXIT"

254
00:16:23,105 --> 00:16:24,540
How much for one elephant?

255
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:27,076
We don't have tickets for elephants!

256
00:16:27,276 --> 00:16:28,711
So it's free, right?

257
00:16:29,044 --> 00:16:30,045
Hey, it's free.

258
00:16:32,982 --> 00:16:34,250
What the...!

259
00:16:47,062 --> 00:16:48,697
You're overfed and overweight!

260
00:16:48,897 --> 00:16:50,766
If you can't get through, this is goodbye.

261
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:52,434
If you're upset, try jumping!

262
00:16:59,708 --> 00:17:00,943
Excuse me, sir.

263
00:17:07,383 --> 00:17:09,251
Sir!

264
00:17:09,451 --> 00:17:11,920
The train will arrive at platform two shortly.

265
00:17:12,121 --> 00:17:13,756
Hurry up, the train is coming!

266
00:17:25,701 --> 00:17:27,136
Let people get off first.

267
00:17:35,277 --> 00:17:37,446
Excuse us, can you make some space?

268
00:17:46,188 --> 00:17:48,257
"SPACE RACETRACK"

269
00:17:57,733 --> 00:17:58,667
Damn it!

270
00:17:59,068 --> 00:18:02,371
What the heck? I've got no luck at all today!

271
00:18:02,838 --> 00:18:03,806
Some god you are!

272
00:18:04,006 --> 00:18:07,009
That old man got my hopes up for nothing.

273
00:18:09,078 --> 00:18:10,345
This is the last 1,000 yen.

274
00:18:10,546 --> 00:18:13,782
If I lose again, we'll have to walk all the way back to Kameari.

275
00:18:16,919 --> 00:18:19,088
If 4-7 wins, the odds are 20 to 1.

276
00:18:19,488 --> 00:18:22,291
But hold on, there's also a chance for 3-6.

277
00:18:22,691 --> 00:18:26,962
People are waiting, so please decide first and line up again.

278
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:34,503
The sixth race will start shortly.

279
00:18:35,804 --> 00:18:38,107
Okay, I'll play it safe with solid 2-5,

280
00:18:38,307 --> 00:18:40,175
to keep my hopes up for the next race.

281
00:18:40,542 --> 00:18:41,944
Okay, 2-5...

282
00:18:44,179 --> 00:18:45,314
1-9, right?

283
00:18:45,514 --> 00:18:47,483
No, not 1-9, 2-5!

284
00:18:49,518 --> 00:18:50,719
Okay, next.

285
00:18:50,953 --> 00:18:52,588
No, not that!

286
00:18:52,821 --> 00:18:54,523
3-7, 3-8, 100 yen.

287
00:18:58,594 --> 00:19:02,131
Shirigomi Stuck and Yamagomorio?

288
00:19:02,331 --> 00:19:03,265
Never heard of them.

289
00:19:03,599 --> 00:19:07,035
What? Both are 9-year-old horses without any pedigree!

290
00:19:07,836 --> 00:19:10,439
Of all things, you made me bet on these old horses!

291
00:19:10,672 --> 00:19:12,241
You're a god of bad luck!

292
00:19:12,441 --> 00:19:13,375
Damn you!

293
00:19:24,586 --> 00:19:26,688
Huh? No way!

294
00:19:29,358 --> 00:19:30,626
"PAYOUT 480 TO 1"

295
00:19:31,593 --> 00:19:33,162
I won!

296
00:19:33,362 --> 00:19:36,431
I won! I won the huge payout!

297
00:19:37,299 --> 00:19:39,201
I won!

298
00:19:46,475 --> 00:19:47,843
You...

299
00:19:58,654 --> 00:20:00,956
You're gonna make me money!

300
00:20:01,957 --> 00:20:03,792
Here you are, Ryo-san.

301
00:20:04,026 --> 00:20:05,394
This is your new bike.

302
00:20:16,605 --> 00:20:18,240
I'm sorry!

303
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:21,143
You're a wonderful elephant!

304
00:20:22,077 --> 00:20:26,148
Okay, I'll treat you to anything you want in return for this winning ticket.

305
00:20:28,517 --> 00:20:32,120
Where did Ryo-chan go with the elephant?

306
00:20:34,323 --> 00:20:38,160
Hello, this is Kameari Park Police Station.

307
00:20:38,493 --> 00:20:39,495
An elephant?

308
00:20:48,303 --> 00:20:52,007
I have a feeling we could be good friends for a long time.

309
00:20:57,946 --> 00:20:59,348
Oh, it's cold!

310
00:21:00,816 --> 00:21:02,184
I'll get you for that.

311
00:21:02,384 --> 00:21:05,087
You rascal!

312
00:21:09,958 --> 00:21:12,928
When I look closely, you've got a cute face.

313
00:21:28,544 --> 00:21:29,378
Tonto!

314
00:21:29,878 --> 00:21:31,013
Tonto?

315
00:21:32,581 --> 00:21:34,116
-Ryotsu! -Chief!

316
00:21:34,316 --> 00:21:38,287
What's the idea of taking an elephant around town?

317
00:21:38,587 --> 00:21:42,157
Just before noon, the police station received a call

318
00:21:42,357 --> 00:21:44,226
that Grand Ueno Zoo had reported him missing.

319
00:21:44,426 --> 00:21:46,595
But you were also missing.

320
00:21:46,828 --> 00:21:50,198
Anyway, I'm glad the elephant and you are safe.

321
00:21:51,533 --> 00:21:53,835
I'm sorry for the trouble.

322
00:21:54,303 --> 00:21:57,573
Apparently, Tonto-chan's mother passed away yesterday.

323
00:22:00,042 --> 00:22:04,513
We zookeepers were so busy taking care of his sick mother

324
00:22:04,713 --> 00:22:07,683
that we completely forgot about Tonto.

325
00:22:08,216 --> 00:22:11,720
He got lonely and escaped from his cage.

326
00:22:12,321 --> 00:22:14,423
Thank you for looking after Tonto.

327
00:22:14,623 --> 00:22:17,459
What are you talking about?

328
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:21,196
Hey, where are you taking my elephant?

329
00:22:21,930 --> 00:22:23,632
Ryotsu! What are you doing?

330
00:22:23,865 --> 00:22:25,100
-Hey, get off me! -Stop!

331
00:22:25,334 --> 00:22:28,637
-Okay, okay, don't be scared. -Hey, what are you doing?

332
00:22:29,071 --> 00:22:31,073
Look, Chief. He doesn't want to go.

333
00:22:31,273 --> 00:22:32,641
I'll keep him!

334
00:22:32,874 --> 00:22:33,575
You idiot!

335
00:22:33,775 --> 00:22:34,876
Nakagawa, come with me!

336
00:22:35,077 --> 00:22:36,178
Y-Yes, sir!

337
00:22:36,378 --> 00:22:37,579
Let me go!

338
00:22:37,779 --> 00:22:38,613
Ryotsu!

339
00:22:38,814 --> 00:22:40,616
Nakagawa, don't let go of him!

340
00:22:40,949 --> 00:22:43,919
Come on, it's dangerous, so just do it now.

341
00:22:44,119 --> 00:22:46,355
Yes! Everyone, please help us.

342
00:22:46,655 --> 00:22:48,824
All right. Leave it to us!

343
00:22:51,827 --> 00:22:53,462
Ready, go!

344
00:22:59,401 --> 00:23:01,803
Stop! Let me go!

345
00:23:02,037 --> 00:23:04,373
You can't separate us now!

346
00:23:07,275 --> 00:23:10,078
Tonto is my elephant!

347
00:23:10,746 --> 00:23:12,814
Ryo-chan has a kind heart.

348
00:23:13,048 --> 00:23:16,585
Tonto-chan will never forget you even when he goes back to the zoo.

349
00:23:21,423 --> 00:23:24,326
Tonto, wait! Tonto!

350
00:23:25,861 --> 00:23:29,164
Don't go, Tonto!

351
00:23:29,665 --> 00:23:30,599
Ryotsu...

352
00:23:30,799 --> 00:23:34,336
Ryo-chan may not look it, but he's actually kind-hearted.

353
00:23:35,070 --> 00:23:37,005
Tonto.

354
00:23:37,472 --> 00:23:38,674
Tell me.

355
00:23:38,874 --> 00:23:42,177
Who's going to win the next Emperor's Cup?

356
00:23:44,413 --> 00:23:47,849
Ryotsu should be kept in the zoo with him.

357
00:23:48,617 --> 00:23:52,254
Tonto, if not the Emperor's Cup, how about the Grand Prix?

358
00:23:52,454 --> 00:23:55,357
Or who'll win the Japanese Derby?

359
00:23:55,557 --> 00:23:57,893
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

360
00:23:58,126 --> 00:24:02,197
CONVENIENCE STORE, STATION, NIKONIKO DORMITORY, BICYCLE, ETC...
